course: dictionary
lesson: 4018
title: Gasp and what it tells you
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing. To find the right meaning, look at the words around the word. «Everyone gasped» in a story means everyone took a sudden, loud breath because they were surprised or shocked.
explain: A gasp is not always about feelings. «Cold water can make the body gasp» is about breathing. Here the body breathes in suddenly on its own, and that can be dangerous, so the words around it tell you this is serious.
explain: Phrases give clues too. «Gasp for air» means struggling to breathe, like after running. «A last-gasp goal» means a goal scored in the final moments, almost too late. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: «Gasp» means to breathe in suddenly and loudly with your mouth open, because of surprise, shock or pain.
fact: «Gasp for air» means to struggle to breathe, for example after running or swimming.
fact: A gasp is a sudden short breath, like «a gasp of horror».
fact: «A last-gasp goal» means a goal scored in the final moments, almost too late.
fact: Cold water can make your body gasp. The RNLI says Float to Live: lean back, spread your arms and legs, float until your breathing calms, then call for help.
exercise: «Everyone gasped» in the story. What does gasped mean here? | Fell asleep in a chair | Ran out of the room | *Took a sudden, loud breath because of surprise | Laughed loudly at a joke
exercise: «A last-gasp goal» means a goal scored when? | *In the final moments, almost too late | In the rain, on a muddy pitch | Before anyone arrived at the field | At the very start of the game
exercise: «Cold water can make the body gasp.» Why is this a serious thing? | It means you need a snack | It means the water is warm and nice | It means you are very happy | *Your body may breathe in suddenly, and you can struggle to breathe
test: «She let out a gasp of horror.» What is a gasp in this sentence? | A loud drum beat | A long, sleepy yawn | *A sudden short breath | A bright flash of light
test: You fall into cold water. The RNLI says what to do first? | Shout and stand up at once | *Lean back, spread your arms and legs, and float until your breathing calms | Swim as fast as you can to the shore without stopping | Dive to the bottom to look for help
exam: «Gasp for air» means what? | To sleep very deeply | *To struggle to breathe, for example after running | To eat a big meal quickly | To laugh until you cry
